Sure.  Longsword does d8 SDAM and d12 LDAM.  An orcish dagger is d3/d3
for both LDAM and SDAM like you said.

On top of that Grimtooth adds "Wielded +d2 to hit and +d6 damage to all
monsters."  It adds a small accuracy and damage bonus that may help a
low level character.

Giantslayer does this, "Wielded
+d5 to hit and x2 damage only against giants, stone giants, hill
giants, fire giants, frost giants, storm giants, giant mummies, giant
zombies, Cyclops, and Lord Surtur. Note that it does not affect ettins
or titans."

Giantslayer is great for giants but otherwise it is a regular longsword
versus everything else.  It is too specialized to be a good artifact.
Good artifacts add damage against everything or do something really
useful.

Look at the Staff, Stormy, Excallibur, Magicbane, Grayswandir,
Snickersnee, and Frosty.  They do extra damage against a wide variety
of monsters, much more than Grimtooth.  That is why they are better.
If you are going for an artifact, get a good one.

As for throwing Grimtooth, sure you can, but in most games it is easier
to get darts or daggers and throw those.



